<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Dutch translation — full UI coverage. Je/jij/jou-form throughout (informal
second-person singular). No u-form anywhere. Brand name "ClothesCast" stays
verbatim.

What is NOT overridden, by design:
- `app_name` — brand identifier, identical across locales.
- `insight_time_am` / `_pm` / `_midnight` / `_noon` (and the *_minutes
  variants) — English-only spoken-time formatter helpers. Dutch locales
  use `insight_time_hour` / `insight_time_hour_minutes` ("%1$d uur" /
  "%1$d:%2$02d") which are translated below; the AM/PM keys exist for
  `Locale.language == "en"` paths only and would never be read in a
  Dutch runtime.

Picker labels under `settings_region_language_*` and
`settings_tts_voice_locale_*` give the Dutch names for every offered
locale (Engels (Verenigde Staten), Frans (Canada), Chinees (vereenvoudigd), …).
The locale tag stored on disk (en-US / fr-CA / zh-CN) is unchanged; only
the displayed label localizes.
-->
